  "$comment": "Consumed by scripts/docs-sync/sync-docs.mjs (see .github/workflows/docs-sync.yml, runs weekly Mon 08:00 UTC). `docs` is the authoritative source of truth: the script hashes the live Markdown of every URL and only regenerates a solution's copy when at least one of its docs actually changed. `productNames` is best-effort only — it is matched against Cloudflare changelog RSS entries purely to annotate the PR description with 'why this ran'; it never gates whether a slug is updated. Edit `docs` whenever a solution should be checked against a different/additional canonical page. Keep every URL under developers.cloudflare.com. `blogTag` links each solution to a pre-verified blog.cloudflare.com/tag/<slug>/ page (rendered on-site as a Dive Deeper link) and is also used by sync-docs.mjs to surface new posts under that tag since the last run — informational only, never auto-added to diveDeeper.blogs. Cloudflare blog tag slugs do not reliably match simple lowercase-hyphenation of the tag name, so verify any new one with curl before adding it.",
